🔴 Fix today (1)

  FortiOS 7.2.5 (Office firewall)
  CVE-2024-21762  Out-of-bounds write in sslvpnd allows remote code execution
    Why   In CISA KEV since 2024-02-09 · ransomware use: known · CISA due date 2024-02-16 · SSVC: exploitation is active · SSVC: automatable · EPSS 94.1% (percentile 100) · public exploit: fortios_sslvpnd · CVSS 9.8 · internet-facing
    Do    Upgrade to 7.2.7 or later (7.2.11 is current in this branch).
    Rule  UNP-KEV, UNP-EXPOSED · verdict affected
    Evidence  CVE.org: affected 7.2.0 to 7.2.6 (CNA Fortinet) (affected)
    Evidence  NVD: cpe:2.3:o:fortinet:fortios up to (excluding) 7.2.7 (affected)
    Rule UNP-KEV  CISA lists this vulnerability in its Known Exploited Vulnerabilities catalog, so attackers are using it now. Fix it today.
    Rule UNP-EXPOSED  This version is affected, the item is marked as internet-facing and the CVSS base score is at or above your exposed threshold (default 7.0). Attackers can reach it, so fix it this week.
    See   https://fortiguard.fortinet.com/psirt/FG-IR-24-015

